{"content":{"activity_type":"event_msg/task_complete","completed_at":1790204543,"duration_ms":23554,"last_agent_message":"Yes—we can preserve the old records and write migrated records alongside them. Git notes are JSONL event sets, so this is structurally possible and safer than destructive replacement.\n\nI’d recommend a parallel-ref migration rather than mixing ev1 and ev2 records in the same live ref:\n\n```text\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger          # new ev2 history, becomes live\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger-ev1      # immutable original snapshot\n```\n\nMigration would:\n\n1. Copy the current notes ref exactly to the ev1 archival ref.\n2. Generate ev2 records from it into a temporary ref.\n3. Verify IDs, links, anchors, counts, and deduplication.\n4. Promote the temporary ev2 ref to the live cledger ref.\n5. Push both refs.\n\nNothing is deleted. The original note blobs and their notes-ref history remain available, and rollback is simply repointing the live ref to the archived one.\n\nI would avoid keeping both generations in the same live note bodies because:\n\n- Every conversation appears twice.\n- Readers must continually suppress ev1 records when an ev2 equivalent exists.\n- Old links target ev1 IDs while new links target ev2 IDs.\n- Scan/export/context consumers may accidentally process both.\n- The transitional compatibility logic becomes permanent.\n\nA separate archival ref provides safety without contaminating normal reads.\n\nWe can make it even safer by retaining two levels:\n\n```text\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger-ev1       # exact old ref\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger-migration # verified candidate\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger           # promoted live ref\n```\n\nThe migration should never mutate the ev1 archive. It should also write a manifest containing only structural information: source and result ref SHAs, event/anchor counts, old→new ID mapping, deduplication counts, dangling-link counts, and tool version. The mapping itself may be important to downstream consumers, so it should be retained as an artifact or migration record.\n\nOne caveat: merely “writing new entries” while leaving the old live ref untouched would not automatically make existing readers use the new generation. We need either:\n\n- promotion of the new ref to the canonical live name, while archiving the old ref; or\n- a configuration change telling all consumers to read a new ref.\n\nPromoting the verified candidate is simpler and keeps existing installations working.\n\nSo yes: preserve everything, migrate additively into a new ref, verify it, then switch the canonical ref pointer. No destructive rewrite or wipe is necessary.","started_at":1790204520,"time_to_first_token_ms":6546,"turn_id":"01a0d081-2734-7b60-bd47-44efe7e3cfa5"},"context":{"branch":"migrate-ev1-to-ev2-additive","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"34960532b3530bb284be0858bd5f7237c8d36f88","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-d9a23dea07eb33611aed2e12709f8c85863d6a83b67082bba2512f332b271f4d","kind":"activity","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-23T23:02:23.802Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"completed_at":1790204543,"duration_ms":23554,"last_agent_message":"Yes—we can preserve the old records and write migrated records alongside them. Git notes are JSONL event sets, so this is structurally possible and safer than destructive replacement.\n\nI’d recommend a parallel-ref migration rather than mixing ev1 and ev2 records in the same live ref:\n\n```text\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger          # new ev2 history, becomes live\nrefs/notes/conversation-ledger-ev1      # immutable original snapshot\n```\n\nMigration would:\n\n1. Copy the current notes ref exactly to the ev1 archival ref.\n2. G